            <div xml:id="d831">

                <pb facs="0911" n="807" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg807"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Woodward Electoral Mission/98a:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Nicaragua</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-06-23T17:00:00-04:00">June 23, 1932—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>60. Personal for Admiral Woodward from the Secretary. I want you to know that we
                    appreciate the difficulties which you may have to face in carrying out the
                    supervision with a possibly reduced and less selective personnel. We made every
                    effort we could to see that you were furnished with the full complement of
                    personnel contemplated by the plan for electoral supervision discussed with you
                    on your last visit to the Department, but circumstances beyond our control have
                    made this impossible. However, I have every confidence that you are going to do
                    an admirable piece of work and give the Nicaraguans a highly satisfactory
                    supervision. You may be assured that we are doing and shall do everything we can
                    to give you full support.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
